@en "net"
@fa "شبکه"
@ar "شبکة"
package net

// This file exists solely as an i18n anchor, not an implementation. The
// raw-socket/TCP/DNS/... functionality that used to live directly in
// std/net/net.salam now lives in std/net/{tcp,dns,internal/rawsock,...} -
// see those packages instead. This stub's only job is to register "net"
// itself as a translatable import segment (@fa "شبکه", @ar "شبکة"): the
// compiler's localized-import resolver (c/src/semantic/sema.c,
// resolve_ident_import/seg_to_canon) builds a dotted path like
// "net.http" one DOT-separated segment at a time, translating each
// segment independently by scanning every std/<dir>/<dir>.salam file for
// an @<lang> tag matching that segment - so "net" needs a package file
// of its own for that segment to resolve in fa/ar at all, even though
// nothing else in this directory tree is "the net package" anymore.
// Deleting this file (as happened when net.salam's old socket code was
// split into subpackages) silently breaks every fa/ar import of any
// net.* subpackage; English is unaffected because it also resolves
// dotted imports directly from the path components, with no alias
// lookup required.
